diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index 3581fd1b1..0d9301656 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -8316,6 +8316,20 @@ Video Sync
     :desync:            Sync video according to system clock, and let audio play
                         on its own.
 
+``--video-sync-experiment=<off|feedback|guarded>``
+    mpv-ht experimental presentation feedback and drift correction (default:
+    ``off``). ``feedback`` validates D3D11 timing and tracks optional Vulkan
+    present-completion counts, retaining the existing drift-correction policy.
+    ``guarded`` additionally filters and bounds corrections with
+    ``--video-sync=display-vdrop``. Inconsistent or unavailable timing falls
+    back to the existing policy. Changing this option recreates the video output.
+
+    Vulkan completion counts are not precise display timestamps. Neither this
+    option nor the ``video-sync-feedback`` property measures acoustic lip-sync.
+    Encoded audio is not resampled. The normal ``off`` path keeps existing
+    timing behavior. This option is experimental and is not a guaranteed cure
+    for stuttering or insufficient rendering performance.
+
 ``--video-sync-max-factor=<value>``
     Maximum multiple for which to try to fit the video's FPS to the display's
     FPS (default: 5).
